  <div class="content-callout">
    <h2>The Short Answer</h2>
    <p>
      <strong>Saily</strong> is the pick if you want a security suite (VPN, ad blocking, malware blocking) baked into the eSIM itself, plus one universal profile that keeps working as you cross borders. <strong>SimLocal</strong> is the pick if you care more about what happens when something goes wrong: an unconditional refund policy, WhatsApp support, and, for a UK trip specifically, a real UK phone number bundled into the plan. Neither of those things shows up on a price chart, so read the differences below before deciding on discount percentage alone.
    </p>
  </div>

